==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈhakə/}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|de|gml|hakke}}, also {{der|de|goh|hakka||animal heel}}, which has no attested continuation in [[w:Middle High German|Middle High German]], however. Ultimately from {{der|de|gem-pro|*hak(k)-|}}, perhaps related to {{m|gem-pro|*hakô}}. Compare {{cog|nl|hak}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# {{lb|de|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany}} [[heel]] (of the foot)
# {{lb|de|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany}} the back of the [[shoe]], which is around the [[heel]] (including or excluding the [[sole]], for which alone {{m|de|Absatz}} is used)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|de|Ferse}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|hacke}}. Pertaining to {{m|de|hacken||to chop}}.

